4799 0 obj<</Title(PART 1 -  GENERAL)/Parent 4797 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 72 689 0]>>/First 4800 0 R/Last 4893 0 R/Count 18/Next 4900 0 R>>
endobj
4800 0 obj<</Title(1.01 SUMMARY)/Parent 4799 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 72 673 0]>>/First 4801 0 R/Last 4804 0 R/Count 4/Next 4805 0 R>>
endobj
4801 0 obj<</Title(A. The requirements listed in this section are supplemental to the Division 01 General Requirements.)/Parent 4800 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 86 658 0]>>/Next 4802 0 R>>
endobj
4802 0 obj<</Title(B. It shall be the responsibility of the Plumbing and Mechanical Contractor to examine and refer to all Architectural, Civil, Structural, Electrical, and Landscape and specifications for construction conditions which may affect the scope of Plumbing and HVAC work.  Inspect the building site and existing facilities for verification of present conditions.  Make proper provisions for these conditions in performance of the work and cost thereof.)/Parent 4800 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 86 631 0]>>/Prev 4801 0 R/Next 4803 0 R>>
endobj
4803 0 obj<</Title(C. Plumbing and Mechanical work for this project shall include all items, articles, materials and the associated labor mentioned, scheduled or shown in these specifications and in the accompanying drawings.)/Parent 4800 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 86 569 0]>>/Prev 4802 0 R/Next 4804 0 R>>
endobj
4804 0 obj<</Title(D. Furnish and install all equipment, materials and any required incidental items required by good practice to complete the systems described herein.)/Parent 4800 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 86 531 0]>>/Prev 4803 0 R>>
endobj
4805 0 obj<</Title(1.02 CODES AND STANDARDS)/Parent 4799 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 72 504 0]>>/Prev 4800 0 R/First 4806 0 R/Last 4806 0 R/Count 1/Next 4807 0 R>>
endobj
4806 0 obj<</Title(A. Work shall meet the requirements of the plans and specifications and shall not be less than the minimum requirements of applicable sections of the latest Codes and Standards of the following Organizations:)/Parent 4805 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 86 488 0]>>>>
endobj
4807 0 obj<</Title(1.03 FEES AND PERMITS)/Parent 4799 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 72 242 0]>>/Prev 4805 0 R/First 4808 0 R/Last 4809 0 R/Count 2/Next 4810 0 R>>
endobj
4808 0 obj<</Title(A. The Plumbing and Mechanical Contractors shall pay all fees and arrange all permits required for work done under their contract and under their supervision by subcontract.)/Parent 4807 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 86 227 0]>>/Next 4809 0 R>>
endobj
4809 0 obj<</Title(B. All usage contracts between the C.O. and the serving utilities company, such as membership and usage charges or fees, etc., for the purpose of obtaining the services for the utility company shall be applied for and paid for by the C.O..)/Parent 4807 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 86 200 0]>>/Prev 4808 0 R>>
endobj
4810 0 obj<</Title(1.04 MATERIALS AND EQUIPMENT)/Parent 4799 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 72 161 0]>>/Prev 4807 0 R/First 4811 0 R/Last 4820 0 R/Count 9/Next 4821 0 R>>
endobj
4811 0 obj<</Title(A. Manufacturer\220s trade names and catalog numbers listed are intended to indicate the quality of equipment or materials desired.  Manufacturers not listed in the specification will be considered substitutions and must have prior approval.)/Parent 4810 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 86 146 0]>>/Next 4812 0 R>>
endobj
4812 0 obj<</Title(B. See Division 01 for Substitutions Procedures. Requests for substitution are to be submitted sufficiently ahead of the deadline, to give ample time for examination. Prior approval request for substitution must indicate the specific item or items to be furnished in lieu of those scheduled, together with complete technical and comparative data on scheduled items and items proposed for substitution.)/Parent 4810 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3315 0 R/XYZ 86 107 0]>>/Prev 4811 0 R/Next 4814 0 R>>
endobj
4814 0 obj<</Title(C. If the engineer approves any proposed substitution, the approved product will be listed in an addendum. Bidders shall not rely on approval made in any other manner.)/Parent 4810 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 685 0]>>/Prev 4812 0 R/Next 4815 0 R>>
endobj
4815 0 obj<</Title(D. Mechanical equipment may be installed with manufacturer\220s standard finish and color except where specific color, finish or choice is indicated.  If the manufacturer has no standard finish, equipment shall have a prime coat and two finish coats of gray enamel.)/Parent 4810 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 658 0]>>/Prev 4814 0 R/Next 4816 0 R>>
endobj
4816 0 obj<</Title(E. High altitude operation: Capacity of all equipment is to be sized and manufactured to perform at the elevation of the project site. If not specifically indicated in the equipment schedule or in the specifications provide all required accessories and equipment for proper operation at elevation of the project site.)/Parent 4810 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 620 0]>>/Prev 4815 0 R/Next 4817 0 R>>
endobj
4817 0 obj<</Title(F. This Contractor shall be responsible for materials and equipment installed under this contract.  Contractor shall also be responsible for the protection of materials and equipment of others from damage as a result of his work.)/Parent 4810 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 570 0]>>/Prev 4816 0 R/Next 4818 0 R>>
endobj
4818 0 obj<</Title(G. Manufactured material and equipment shall be applied, installed, connected, erected, used, cleaned and conditioned as directed by manufacturer unless herein specified to the contrary.)/Parent 4810 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 531 0]>>/Prev 4817 0 R/Next 4819 0 R>>
endobj
4819 0 obj<</Title(H. This Contractor shall make the required arrangement with the General Contractor or Construction Manager for the introduction into the building of equipment too large to pass through finished openings.)/Parent 4810 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 504 0]>>/Prev 4818 0 R/Next 4820 0 R>>
endobj
4820 0 obj<</Title(I. Store materials and equipment indoors at the job site. If this is not possible, store on raised platforms and protect from the weather by means of waterproof covers. Coverings shall permit circulation of air around the materials to prevent condensation of moisture.  Screen or cap openings in equipment to prevent the entry of vermin.)/Parent 4810 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 466 0]>>/Prev 4819 0 R>>
endobj
4821 0 obj<</Title(1.05 INTENT OF DRAWINGS)/Parent 4799 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 72 416 0]>>/Prev 4810 0 R/First 4822 0 R/Last 4822 0 R/Count 1/Next 4823 0 R>>
endobj
4822 0 obj<</Title(A. The drawings are diagrammatic and do not necessarily show exact location of piping and ductwork unless specifically dimensioned. Riser and other diagrams are schematic and do not necessarily show the physical arrangement of the equipment. They shall not be used for obtaining lineal runs of piping or ductwork, nor shall they be used for shop drawings for piping and ductwork fabrication or ordering. Discrepancies shown on different plans, or between plans and actual field conditions shall be brought to the attention of the C.O. for resolution.)/Parent 4821 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 400 0]>>>>
endobj
4823 0 obj<</Title(1.06 COMMISSIONING OF SYSTEMS)/Parent 4799 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 72 327 0]>>/Prev 4821 0 R/First 4824 0 R/Last 4825 0 R/Count 2/Next 4826 0 R>>
endobj
4824 0 obj<</Title(A. Mechanical systems with a total cooling capacity exceeding 480,000 Btu/hr or a combined heating and service water-heating capacity exceeding 600,000 Btu/hr shall be commissioned by a registered professional in accordance with Section C408 of the International Energy Conservation Code. The mechanical contractor shall correct all installation deficiencies identified by the commissioning agent at no cost to the C.O..)/Parent 4823 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 312 0]>>/Next 4825 0 R>>
endobj
4825 0 obj<</Title(B. See Sections 019113 \215Commissioning Requirements of Contractor\216, 220800 \215Commissioning of Plumbing\216, 230800 \215Commissioning of HVAC\216, 260800 \215Commissioning of Electrical Systems\216.)/Parent 4823 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 250 0]>>/Prev 4824 0 R>>
endobj
4826 0 obj<</Title(1.07 RESPONSIBILITY)/Parent 4799 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 72 223 0]>>/Prev 4823 0 R/First 4827 0 R/Last 4842 0 R/Count 15/Next 4843 0 R>>
endobj
4827 0 obj<</Title(A. Plumbing and HVAC work shall conform to requirements of all divisions 22 and 23 specifications.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 208 0]>>/Next 4828 0 R>>
endobj
4828 0 obj<</Title(B. The Plumbing and Mechanical Contractors shall be responsible for the installation of a satisfactory and complete system in accordance with the intent of the drawing and specifications. Provide, at no extra cost, all incidental items, materials, accessories and labor required for completion of the work even though they are not specifically mentioned or indicated on the drawings or in the specifications.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 181 0]>>/Prev 4827 0 R/Next 4829 0 R>>
endobj
4829 0 obj<</Title(C. The drawings do not attempt to show complete details of the building construction which affect the mechanical and plumbing installation; and reference is therefore required to the Architectural, Civil, Structural, Landscape and Electrical drawings and specifications and to shop drawings of all trades for additional details which affect the installation of the work covered under this Division of the Contract.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3328 0 R/XYZ 86 119 0]>>/Prev 4828 0 R/Next 4831 0 R>>
endobj
4831 0 obj<</Title(D. Location of mechanical and plumbing system components shall be checked for conflicts with openings, structural members and components of other systems having fixed locations. In the event of any conflicts, the C.O. shall be consulted, and their decision shall govern. Necessary changes shall be made at the Contractor\220s expense.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 697 0]>>/Prev 4829 0 R/Next 4832 0 R>>
endobj
4832 0 obj<</Title(E. Determine, and be responsible for, the proper location and character of inserts for hangers, chases, sleeves, and other openings in the construction required for the work and obtain this information well in advance of the construction progress so work will not be delayed.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 647 0]>>/Prev 4831 0 R/Next 4833 0 R>>
endobj
4833 0 obj<</Title(F. Final location of inserts, hangers, etc., required for each installation, must be coordinated with facilities required for other installations to prevent interference.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 608 0]>>/Prev 4832 0 R/Next 4834 0 R>>
endobj
4834 0 obj<</Title(G. Take extreme caution not to install work that connects to equipment until such time as complete Shop Drawings of such equipment have been approved by the C.O..  Any work installed by the Contractor, prior to approval of Shop Drawings, will be at the Contractor's risk.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 581 0]>>/Prev 4833 0 R/Next 4835 0 R>>
endobj
4835 0 obj<</Title(H. All modifications and changes required due to installation of equipment other than the scheduled equipment shall be made at the contractor\220s expense.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 543 0]>>/Prev 4834 0 R/Next 4836 0 R>>
endobj
4836 0 obj<</Title(I. It shall be the responsibility of the installing contractor to coordinate changes to work by other trades that result from the installation of equipment other than the scheduled equipment.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 516 0]>>/Prev 4835 0 R/Next 4837 0 R>>
endobj
4837 0 obj<</Title(J. If the provided equipment is heavier or larger than the scheduled or specified equipment, it shall be the responsibility of the installing contractor to coordinate the required structural changes and pay for any and all associated cost.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 489 0]>>/Prev 4836 0 R/Next 4838 0 R>>
endobj
4838 0 obj<</Title(K. If the provided equipment has different motor characteristics or electrical requirements than the scheduled or specified equipment, it shall be the responsibility of the installing contractor to coordinate the required changes and pay for any and all associated cost.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 450 0]>>/Prev 4837 0 R/Next 4839 0 R>>
endobj
4839 0 obj<</Title(L. If larger or additional electrical conduits, wire or breakers are required due to the installation of equipment other than the scheduled or specified equipment it shall be the responsibility of the installing contractor to coordinate the required changes and pay for any and all associated cost.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 412 0]>>/Prev 4838 0 R/Next 4840 0 R>>
endobj
4840 0 obj<</Title(M. If the provided equipment requires different fluid flow rates than the scheduled or specified equipment, it shall be the responsibility of the installing contractor to coordinate all required changes including but not limited to pumps, piping, valves, etc and pay for any and all associated cost.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 373 0]>>/Prev 4839 0 R/Next 4841 0 R>>
endobj
4841 0 obj<</Title(N. At all times during the performance of this Contract, properly protect work from damage and protect the C.O.'s property from injury of loss.  Make good any damage, injury or loss, except such as may be directly due to errors in the Bidding Documents or caused by Agents or Employees of the C.O..  Adequately protect adjacent property as provided by law and the Bidding Documents. Provide and maintain passageways, guard fences, lights and other facilities for protection required by Public Authority or Local conditions.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 323 0]>>/Prev 4840 0 R/Next 4842 0 R>>
endobj
4842 0 obj<</Title(O. The Contractor shall be responsible for damages incurred due to the work of their contractors, to the building or its contents, people, etc.)/Parent 4826 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 250 0]>>/Prev 4841 0 R>>
endobj
4843 0 obj<</Title(1.08 REVIEW)/Parent 4799 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 72 223 0]>>/Prev 4826 0 R/First 4844 0 R/Last 4844 0 R/Count 1/Next 4845 0 R>>
endobj
4844 0 obj<</Title(A. All work and material is subject to review at any time by the C.O. or his representative. If the C.O. or his representative finds material that does not conform to these specifications or that is not properly installed or finished, correct the deficiencies in a manner satisfactory to the C.O. at the Contractor\220s expense.)/Parent 4843 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 208 0]>>>>
endobj
4845 0 obj<</Title(1.09 WORKMANSHIP)/Parent 4799 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 72 158 0]>>/Prev 4843 0 R/First 4846 0 R/Last 4849 0 R/Count 3/Next 4850 0 R>>
endobj
4846 0 obj<</Title(A. Work under this contract shall be performed by workmen skilled in the particular trade, including work necessary to properly complete the installation in a workmanlike manner to present a neat and finished appearance.)/Parent 4845 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 142 0]>>/Next 4847 0 R>>
endobj
4847 0 obj<</Title(B. Obtain Architect's/Engineer's approval before performing any cutting on structural members or patching of building surfaces. Any damage to the building or equipment by the Mechanical or Plumbing Contractor shall be the responsibility of the Mechanical or Plumbing Contractor and shall be repaired by skilled craftsmen of the trades involved at the Contractor\220s expense.)/Parent 4845 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3331 0 R/XYZ 86 104 0]>>/Prev 4846 0 R/Next 4849 0 R>>
endobj
4849 0 obj<</Title(C. Chases, openings, sleeves, hangers, anchors, recesses, equipment pads, and framing for equipment; shall be provided by others only if so noted on the drawings. Otherwise, they will be provided by the Mechanical or Plumbing Contractor for their work.)/Parent 4845 0 R/A<</S/GoTo/D[3334 0 R/XYZ 86 697 0]>>/Prev 4847 0 R>>
endobj
