8004 0 obj<</Title(B. All refrigerant pipe, elbows and valves shall be individually insulated with no air gaps. Insulation R-value shall not be less than 0.245 btu/hr*ft2*F \(1/2\216 closed cell elastomeric or EDM\). In no case shall the insulation be allowed to be compressed at any point in the system. All joints shall be glued and sealed per insulation manufactures instructions to make an air tight assembly.)/Parent 8001 0 R/A 8003 0 R/Prev 8002 0 R/Next 8005 0 R>>
endobj
8005 0 obj<</Title(C. The piping system shall be designed with pipe expansion and contraction possibilities in mind. Required expansion devices shall be field designed, supplied and installed based on proper evaluation of the proposed piping design. In addition to these requirements, the piping system installation must conform to the equipment manufacturer\220s published guidelines.)/Parent 8001 0 R/A 8003 0 R/Prev 8004 0 R/Next 8006 0 R>>
endobj
8006 0 obj<</Title(D. The installation of pipe hangers, supports, insulation, and in general the methods chosen to attach the pipe system to the structure must allow for expansion and contraction of the piping system and shall not interfere with that movement.)/Parent 8001 0 R/A 8003 0 R/Prev 8005 0 R>>
endobj
