8135 0 obj<</Title(B. NFPA Compliance: Comply with NFPA 654 and NFPA 664 for design, fabrication, and installation of dust collection systems in wood working facilities. Comply with NFPA 69 Standard on Explosion Protection Systems and NFPA 68 Standard on Explosion Protection by Deflagration Venting.)/Parent 8133 0 R/A 8124 0 R/Prev 8134 0 R/Next 8136 0 R>>
endobj
8136 0 obj<</Title(C. ASHRAE Compliance: Applicable requirements in ASHRAE 62.1-2004, Section 5 - "Systems and Equipment" and Section 7 - "Construction and Startup.")/Parent 8133 0 R/A 8124 0 R/Prev 8135 0 R/Next 8137 0 R>>
endobj
8137 0 obj<</Title(D. Comply with NFPA 70 and NFPA 496.)/Parent 8133 0 R/A 8124 0 R/Prev 8136 0 R>>
endobj
8138 0 obj<</Title(1.04 WARRANTY)/Parent 8126 0 R/A 8124 0 R/Prev 8133 0 R/First 8139 0 R/Last 8139 0 R/Count 1>>
endobj
8139 0 obj<</Title(A. Manufacture\220s standard warranty.)/Parent 8138 0 R/A 8124 0 R>>
endobj
8140 0 obj<</Title(PART 2 -  PRODUCTS)/Parent 8125 0 R/A 8124 0 R/Prev 8126 0 R/First 8141 0 R/Last 8160 0 R/Count 4/Next 8166 0 R>>
endobj
8141 0 obj<</Title(2.01 GENERAL)/Parent 8140 0 R/A 8124 0 R/First 8142 0 R/Last 8142 0 R/Count 1/Next 8144 0 R>>
endobj
8142 0 obj<</Title(A. Furnish a completely packaged, fully assembled, pre-wired, inclusive of remote mounted control package, dust collector complying with the performance conditions listed in the mechanical drawings and schedules. The collector shall be a vertical cartridge dust collector with over-bags, designed to collect, filter and store dust coming from wood working equipment. The manufacturer of collector must be certified to make, assemble and distribute industrial air purification equipment. The dust collector must be made in accordance with safety rules and regulations. Written verification that the collector and deflagration isolation devices and all other safety devices used have been tested as such, and are in compliance with NFPA standards, must be available from the dust collector manufacturer.)/Parent 8141 0 R/A 8124 0 R>>
endobj
8143 0 obj<</S/GoTo/D[6225 0 R/Fit]>>
endobj
8144 0 obj<</Title(2.02 MANUFACTURERS)/Parent 8140 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8141 0 R/First 8145 0 R/Last 8146 0 R/Count 2/Next 8147 0 R>>
endobj
8145 0 obj<</Title(A. Aget Manufacturing Company)/Parent 8144 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Next 8146 0 R>>
endobj
8146 0 obj<</Title(B. All other manufacturers MUST submit for alternate approval prior to bid, in accordance with bid documents \215Substitution Request\216.)/Parent 8144 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8145 0 R>>
endobj
8147 0 obj<</Title(2.03 DUST COLLECTOR)/Parent 8140 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8144 0 R/First 8148 0 R/Last 8159 0 R/Count 12/Next 8160 0 R>>
endobj
8148 0 obj<</Title(A. Job installation and units will conform to NFPA 664.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Next 8149 0 R>>
endobj
8149 0 obj<</Title(B. See plans schedule for performance specifications and characteristics.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8148 0 R/Next 8150 0 R>>
endobj
8150 0 obj<</Title(C. The dust collector fan shall be located on the "clean air side" of the cyclone.  The fan shall be constructed of spark-resistant aluminum alloy, shall be a "backward inclined" design high-efficiency fan wheel, and shall rotate at a nominal speed of 3600 rpm in a direct drive configuration.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8149 0 R/Next 8151 0 R>>
endobj
8151 0 obj<</Title(D. The cyclone unit shall be driven by premium efficiency nema frame motor. Additionally, the motor shall incorporate an umbrella type weather cap assembly, to protect the motor from rain, ice, or snow.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8150 0 R/Next 8152 0 R>>
endobj
8152 0 obj<</Title(E. The cyclone shall be a high efficiency design and shall incorporate straightening vanes in the cyclone stack to optimize fan performance.  Additionally, the cyclone shall be constructed in a component bolt-together design of heavy gauge aisi 1010 cq cold rolled steel.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8151 0 R/Next 8153 0 R>>
endobj
8153 0 obj<</Title(F. The cyclone shall incorporate a pressure relief door to relieve the cyclone of a rapid rise in internal pressure in the event of an explosion.  The door shall incorporate stainless steel retaining springs and hinge, and shall be sized to provide a minimum of one \(1\) square foot of vent opening for every 20-30 cubic feet of internal cyclone volume.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8152 0 R/Next 8154 0 R>>
endobj
8154 0 obj<</Title(G. The cyclone unit shall incorporate a supporting angle iron framework, lending support at both the base of the cone and at the base of the cylinder.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8153 0 R/Next 8155 0 R>>
endobj
8155 0 obj<</Title(H. The cyclone unit shall be mounted on a supporting welded angle iron stand.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8154 0 R/Next 8156 0 R>>
endobj
8156 0 obj<</Title(I. Collected dust shall be deposited into one of the following types of dust storage containers)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8155 0 R/Next 8157 0 R>>
endobj
8157 0 obj<</Title(J. Single 55-gallon drum, containing 7.3 cu. Ft. Dust storage capacity.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8156 0 R/Next 8158 0 R>>
endobj
8158 0 obj<</Title(K. Units depositing collected dust into standard 55 gallon drums shall incorporate a positive sealing clamp-on drum cover assembly.  Those held on by dust collector suction only are not acceptable.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8157 0 R/Next 8159 0 R>>
endobj
8159 0 obj<</Title(L. The cyclone unit dust collector shall be supplied with a minimum of one coat of super-durable polyester tgic-free powder coating, ral 7015gl.)/Parent 8147 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8158 0 R>>
endobj
8160 0 obj<</Title(2.04 DUST COLLECTOR ACCESSORIES:)/Parent 8140 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8147 0 R/First 8161 0 R/Last 8165 0 R/Count 5>>
endobj
8161 0 obj<</Title(A. \(1\) 55-gallon drums shall be provided with the dust collector.)/Parent 8160 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Next 8162 0 R>>
endobj
8162 0 obj<</Title(B. Factory installed magnehelic gage to read the pressure across the main filter cartridge.)/Parent 8160 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8161 0 R/Next 8163 0 R>>
endobj
8163 0 obj<</Title(C. Explosion Isolation Valve to be installed on the dirty air inlet:)/Parent 8160 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8162 0 R/Next 8164 0 R>>
endobj
8164 0 obj<</Title(D. Slide gates at each woodworking equipment.)/Parent 8160 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8163 0 R/Next 8165 0 R>>
endobj
8165 0 obj<</Title(E. Refer to schedules on mechanical drawings for any additional information and accessories.)/Parent 8160 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8164 0 R>>
endobj
8166 0 obj<</Title(PART 3 -  EXECUTION)/Parent 8125 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Prev 8140 0 R/First 8167 0 R/Last 8178 0 R/Count 2>>
endobj
8167 0 obj<</Title(3.01 INSTALLATION)/Parent 8166 0 R/A 8143 0 R/First 8168 0 R/Last 8177 0 R/Count 9/Next 8178 0 R>>
endobj
8168 0 obj<</Title(A. Assembly dust collection unit per the manufacture\220s installation guidelines.)/Parent 8167 0 R/A 8143 0 R/Next 8170 0 R>>
endobj
8169 0 obj<</S/GoTo/D[6228 0 R/Fit]>>
endobj
8170 0 obj<</Title(B. Install in accordance with manufacturer\220s Installation & Maintenance instructions.)/Parent 8167 0 R/A 8169 0 R/Prev 8168 0 R/Next 8171 0 R>>
endobj
8171 0 obj<</Title(C. Use all factory provided lifting lugs to rig the units or modules. Ensure that spreader bars are used to prevent damaging the cabinets.)/Parent 8167 0 R/A 8169 0 R/Prev 8170 0 R/Next 8172 0 R>>
endobj
8172 0 obj<</Title(D. Lift modules in an upright position.)/Parent 8167 0 R/A 8169 0 R/Prev 8171 0 R/Next 8173 0 R>>
endobj
8173 0 obj<</Title(E. Level unit horizontally and vertically, using steel shims under legs where required. Shims shall have a corrosion resistant coating.)/Parent 8167 0 R/A 8169 0 R/Prev 8172 0 R/Next 8174 0 R>>
endobj
8174 0 obj<</Title(F. Contractor shall protect the dust collector inlet and outlet during construction to prevent construction debris from entering the collector prior to making duct connection to the unit. Do not operate fan system until filters are in place.)/Parent 8167 0 R/A 8169 0 R/Prev 8173 0 R/Next 8175 0 R>>
endobj
8175 0 obj<</Title(G. Connect exhaust and return ducts to dust collection unit, flexible connections shall not be used.)/Parent 8167 0 R/A 8169 0 R/Prev 8174 0 R/Next 8176 0 R>>
endobj
8176 0 obj<</Title(H. Perform preliminary start-up unit check per the dust collector manufacture\220s installation guidelines.)/Parent 8167 0 R/A 8169 0 R/Prev 8175 0 R/Next 8177 0 R>>
endobj
8177 0 obj<</Title(I. Check fan motors for rotation and amp draw for each phase. Record information on the start-up data sheets.)/Parent 8167 0 R/A 8169 0 R/Prev 8176 0 R>>
endobj
8178 0 obj<</Title(3.02 FACTORY START-UP AND VERIFICATION)/Parent 8166 0 R/A 8169 0 R/Prev 8167 0 R/First 8179 0 R/Last 8179 0 R/Count 1>>
endobj
8179 0 obj<</Title(A. Factory trained technicians shall inspect and commission all components including:)/Parent 8178 0 R/A 8169 0 R>>
endobj
