endobj
10381 0 obj<</Title(D. EXISTING ELECTRICAL SERVICE)/Parent 10376 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Prev 10380 0 R>>
endobj
10382 0 obj<</Title(3.03 COORDINATION)/Parent 10371 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Prev 10376 0 R/First 10383 0 R/Last 10386 0 R/Count 4/Next 10387 0 R>>
endobj
10383 0 obj<</Title(A. The Contractor is responsible for providing and coordinating phased activities and construction methods that minimize disruption to facility operations. Ensure that any portion of systems or devices to remain continue to be complete and operational. Equipment and devices shall not be removed or reconfigured until coordinated with C.O.)/Parent 10382 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Next 10384 0 R>>
endobj
10384 0 obj<</Title(B. The Contractor shall coordinate interfaces to existing systems that are being demolished in order to minimize disruption to the existing systems operations. Coordinate all utility service and system outages with the C.O. and the local Utility Company as applicable.)/Parent 10382 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Prev 10383 0 R/Next 10385 0 R>>
endobj
10385 0 obj<</Title(C. Demolition and remodel shall be done quickly so as to not hinder other trades.)/Parent 10382 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Prev 10384 0 R/Next 10386 0 R>>
endobj
10386 0 obj<</Title(D. Refer to demolition drawings, new drawings and site drawings to coordinate demolition and remodel efforts. Notify C.O. of any discrepancies.)/Parent 10382 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Prev 10385 0 R>>
endobj
10387 0 obj<</Title(3.04 EXISTING SERVICES/SYSTEMS TO REMAIN - Maintain services/systems indicated to remain and protect them against damage.)/Parent 10371 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Prev 10382 0 R/First 10388 0 R/Last 10390 0 R/Count 3/Next 10391 0 R>>
endobj
10388 0 obj<</Title(A. Comply with requirements for existing services/systems interruptions.)/Parent 10387 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Next 10389 0 R>>
endobj
10389 0 obj<</Title(B. When temporary bypass systems are installed, test and get approval from C.O. before proceeding with demolition of existing systems.)/Parent 10387 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Prev 10388 0 R/Next 10390 0 R>>
endobj
10390 0 obj<</Title(C. For existing equipment cabinets with active components in them, provide an air tight dust seal around the cabinet and circulate cooling air with a portable air conditioning unit or other means to ensure equipment does not overheat.)/Parent 10387 0 R/A 10379 0 R/Prev 10389 0 R>>
endobj
